anager","rationale":"Chosen as an evaluation corpus because it packs three services, a substantial cross-language test suite, 17 Alembic migrations, and a clean three-tier architecture into one repo, giving a clear ground truth for community detection.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":"https://github.com/glitchwerks/rsl-siege-manager"},{"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-05-15","contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_review","label":"Review: rsl-siege-manager","rationale":"Evaluates only the headline outputs of GRAPH_REPORT.md against a single criterion — would a developer familiar with the codebase nominate these as core, surprising, or worth investigating — quoting the report so each finding is verifiable against committed artifacts.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-05-13","contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graph_report","label":"graphify GRAPH_REPORT for rsl-siege-manager","rationale":null,"source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/GRAPH_REPORT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graph_json","label":"graph.json (graph data for graphify query)","rationale":null,"source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/graph.json","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graph_html","label":"graph.html (interactive force-directed visualization)","rationale":null,"source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/graph.html","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_manifest_json","label":"manifest.json (per-file extraction record)","rationale":null,"source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/manifest.json","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graphify","label":"graphify CLI","rationale":"Uses tree-sitter for code (free, fast) and reserves LLM API calls for non-code files, so cost on a code-heavy repo is dominated by docs.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":"https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify"},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graphifyy_package","label":"graphifyy (PyPI package)","rationale":null,"source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":"https://pypi.org/project/graphifyy/"},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_graphifyignore","label":".graphifyignore filter","rationale":"Documented mitigation for test-fixture god nodes and docstring isolated nodes: excluding tests/, __tests__/ and alembic/versions/ removes that class of false positive materially.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_finding_1_test_fixture_god_nodes","label":"Finding 1 — Test fixtures dominate core abstractions","rationale":"Degree centrality saturates test factories by design: factories create the primary domain objects every test exercises, so better coverage means more accumulated edges.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":"Finding 1","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_finding_2_entry_points_and_utilities","label":"Finding 2 — Without tests, god nodes mix domain types with entry points and utilities","rationale":"React page components rank high because entry points import many things, and cn() ranks high because the React+Tailwind idiom makes every component import it — connection count reflects structural pattern, not semantic importance.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":"Finding 2","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_finding_3_cross_language_inferred","label":"Finding 3 — Surprising connections cross language boundaries","rationale":"Python classes cannot use TypeScript types at runtime; these are name-based similarity matches between identically-named constructs, so monorepos with shared domain vocabulary should expect a high false-positive rate here.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":"Finding 3","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_finding_4_low_cohesion","label":"Finding 4 — Community cohesion is uniformly low on this corpus","rationale":"Community detection does not recover the clean three-service architecture; candidate causes are INFERRED cross-language edges diluting cluster signal, parameters favouring over-segmentation at this density, or genuinely absent intra-cluster topology.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":"Finding 4","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"worked_rsl_siege_manager_finding_5_migration_docstrings","label":"Finding 5 — Alembic migration docstrings surface as isolated nodes","rationale":"The 'possible documentation gaps or missing edges' label misleads here because migration and pytest docstrings are change annotations or test descriptions, not architectural entities with missing connections.","source_file":"worked/rsl-siege-manager/review.md","source_location":"Finding 5","source_url":null},{"author":null,"cap